    "question": "Mr. and Mrs. McPherson have to renew their rent by the end of the year. They agreed that Mrs. McPherson would raise 30% of the money. If their rent is $1200 per year, how much does Mr. McPherson need to raise to complete the rent?",
    "gold": "840",
    "answer": "30% of $1200 is (30/100)*$1200 = $<<(30/100)*1200=360>>360\nMrs. McPherson will pay $360 leaving $1200-$360 = $<<1200-360=840>>840 which Mr. McPherson will have to raise\n#### 840"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Mr. McPherson needs to raise to complete the rent, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the amount Mrs. McPherson will raise.\n2. Subtract the amount Mrs. McPherson will raise from the total rent to find out how much Mr. McPherson needs to raise.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the amount Mrs. McPherson will raise. Mrs. McPherson agreed to raise 30% of the rent. The total rent is $1200 per year. Therefore, we calculate 30% of $1200 as follows:\n\n\\[ 30\\% \\text{ of } 1200 = 0.30 \\times 1200 = 360 \\]\n\nSo, Mrs. McPherson will raise $360.\n\nNext, we need to find out how much Mr. McPherson needs to raise. We do this by subtracting the amount Mrs. McPherson will raise from the total rent:\n\n\\[ 1200 - 360 = 840 \\]\n\nTherefore, Mr. McPherson needs to raise \\(\\boxed{840}\\).",
